---
import Layout from "@/layouts/page-layout.astro";
import NavLink from "@/components/nav-link.astro";
---

<Layout title="Linguistic Search">
  <div class="md:w-5/6 mx-auto md:p-6 p-2">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center justify-start mb-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl shadow bg-brand-100 p-1">
        <NavLink reload href="/advanced-search" class="text-xl md:text-3xl font-semibold p-3 text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-500">
            Faceted Search
            </NavLink>
            <h2 class="bg-brand-50 text-xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-brand-600 rounded-2xl p-3">
        Linguistic Search
      </h2>
    </div>

  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm ">  
      <!-- Intro note -->
    
    <!-- text normalisation Note -->       
       <details  class="mb-4 p-4 bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-300 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-semibold text-yellow-800 cursor-pointer">Text normalisation</summary>
        <div class="text-sm grid gap-1 pt-2">  
          <p>To make linguistic searching more consistent across the corpus, we have normalised the spelling of all passages.  
          The current normalisation applies the following transformations:
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-600">  
            <li><strong>ae</strong> and <strong>oe</strong> are normalised to <strong>e</strong>;</li>
            <li><strong>y</strong> and <strong>j</strong> are normalised to <strong>i</strong>;</li>
            <li><strong>v</strong> is generally normalised to <strong>u</strong>, except when it occurs at the beginning of a word followed by a vowel, or mid-word between two vowels.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Users should keep these normalisations in mind when formulating linguistic searches, as the searchable text may differ from the spelling found in the original manuscript or edition. Example: you will find no matches when searching for 'ciuitas', since all instances of the word are normalised to 'civitas'.
          For more details see the <NavLink href="/about/technical">technical implementation</NavLink>.
        </p>
        </div>
      </details>
     <!-- Search Guide -->
    <details open class="mb-4 p-4 bg-orange-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-lg group">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-lg cursor-pointer text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-800">
     How to use the linguistic search
      </summary>
      
      <p class="p-3 text-brand-800 font-normal">The linguistic search provides a more flexible way to search the corpus of passages by querying the linguistic structure and wording of the texts. 
        In contrast to the faceted search, which filters passages by predefined metadata categories, the linguistic search allows you to search for specific lemmas, phrases, or more complex linguistic 
        patterns using Simple, Phrase, Lemma, and CQL search.
 </p>
      <div class=" grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(20rem,1fr))] gap-4 text-sm">
     <!-- Search Modes -->
     <div>
      <p class=" text-base text-brand-800 py-2">Select one of the <span class="decoration underline underline-offset-2">four</span> search modes available in the drop down menu below:</p>
       <ul class="pt-3 space-y-2 ml-4 list-decimal">
         <li>
           <span class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Simple mode:</span> Search for a <strong>single</strong> word e.g. <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">Jerusalem</code>
           or
           <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">.*rusalem</code>
          <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">shows all occurrences of the word with the exact same spelling or with variations when using wild cards (see further below).</span>

         </li>
         <li>
           <span class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Phrase:</span> Search for a whole phrase e.g. <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">reliqua pedibus suis</code>
          <br> <span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">shows all occurrences of the phrase in exactly this order and with the exact same spelling or with variants when using wild cards.</span>
         </li>
         <li>
           <span class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Lemma:</span> Search for a <strong>single</strong> lemma e.g. <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">pes</code>
           <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">shows all forms of the word like 'pes', 'pedibus' etc.</span>
         </li>
         <li>
             <span class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Corpus Query Language (CQL): </span>
             <ul class="space-y-2 ml-4 font-medium list-disc pt-2">
                 
                  <li>
                 Search by word case insensitive: <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[lc="operatus"]</code>
                 <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds words "operatus" (lower case) and "Operatus" (upper case).</span>
                 </li>                            
               
                 <li>
                 Search for several words (OR): <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[word="populus|civitatem"]</code>
                 <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds the words"populus" <strong>OR</strong> "civitatem"</span>
                 </li>
                 <li>
                  Search for several words (AND) | Searching with Word Distance
                  <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">find two words or two lemmata, or a word and a lemma within a certain distance from each other:</span>
                  <ul class="space-y-2 ml-4 list-disc list-inside">
                      <li>
                        <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[word="rege"][word="Francorum"]</code>
                        <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds "rege" immediately followed by "Francorum"</span>
                      </li>
                      <li>
                          <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[word="rege"][][word=".*ilippo"]</code>
                          <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds "rege" exactly 1 word away from words ending with "ilippo" (like "Phillipo", "philippo", "Filippo" etc.)</span>
                      </li>
                      <li>
                        <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[word="decem"][]&#123;0,15&#125;[word="tribu.*"]</code>
                        <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds the word "decem" within 0 to 15 words away from words starting with "tribu" (like "tribus" or "tribubus")</span>
                      </li>
                      <li>
                        <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">q[lemma="cedo"][]&#123;0,15&#125;[lc="roman.*"]</code>
                        <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">finds the lemma "cedo" within 0 to 15 words away from words (case-insensitive) starting with "roman" (like "romanus", "Romanus" or "romanorumque")</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                 </li>
             </ul>
         </li>
          
       </ul>
     </div>
     <div class="grid content-between">
       <!-- Wildcards -->
       <div>
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Using Wildcards with any of the four modes</h3>
         <ul class="space-y-2 ml-4">
           <li>
             <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">.</code> (dot) = matches any <strong>single</strong> character
             <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">Example: <code class="bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.erusalem</code> matches "Jerusalem" or "Ierusalem"</span>
           </li>
           <li>
             <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">.*</code> (dot-asterisk) = matches <strong>any number</strong> of characters (including zero)
             <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">Example: <code class="bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.*erusalem</code> matches "Jerusalem", "Hierusalem", "Ierusalem"</span>
           </li>
           <li>
             <code class="bg-white px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs">.?</code> (dot-question) = matches <strong>zero or one</strong> character
             <br><span class="text-gray-600 text-xs">Example: <code class="bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.?elio</code> matches "elio" or "helio"</span>
           </li>
         </ul>
       </div>
       <!-- Quick Examples -->
       <div>
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-700 mb-2">Quick Examples</h3>
         <div class="bg-white p-3 rounded border border-gray-200">
           <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
             <li>Simple: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 text-xs  rounded-md">Jerusalem</code></li>
             <li>Simple with wildcard: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.*erusalem</code></li>
             <li>Phrase: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">decem trib.*</code></li>
             <li>Lemma: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">altissimus</code></li>
             <li>CQL multiple words: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">q[word="templum|ecclesia|synagoga"]</code></li>
             <li>CQL with distance: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">q[lemma="sacerdos"][]&#123;0,15&#125; [word="sanguis"]</code></li>
             <li>CQL with distance in combination with case-insensitive mode: <code class="border bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">q[word="rege"][lc="Francorum"]</code></li>
           </ul>
         </div>
       </div>
     </div>
    </div>
    </details>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr_auto] gap-2">
      <select id="search-type-select" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-lg p-2">
     <option value="simple">Simple</option>
     <option value="phrase">Phrase</option>
     <option value="lemma">Lemma</option>
     <option value="cql">CQL</option>
      </select>
      <input type="text" id="search-input" class="w-full p-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg"/>
      <button id="search-button" class="button-custom rounded-lg">Search</button>
    </div>
    
    <div id="stats" class="py-2 text-center"></div>
    <div id="results" class="bg-white"></div>
    <div id="pagination"></div>
  </div>
</div>
    
</Layout>

<script src="@/lib/noske/noske-search.js"></script>
